{
  format: 1
  name: role-view-parameter-inferred-typing
  suite: scenario
  spec: ["#interfaces", "§10.1", "#mutations", "§8.3", "#clients", "§12.1"]
  tags: ["typing", "authz", "boundary"]
  note: '''
    The ROLE-granted surface path of §10.1's inferred view parameter — the
    counterpart of `06/surface-view-parameter-inferred-typing`. A surface `$view`
    parameter "is inferred exactly as a mutation parameter is (§8.3)", and that
    holds however the surface is exposed: the role surface `by_state` declares no
    `$params`, the filter `t.done == @done` compares `@done` against the `bool`
    field `tasks.done`, so `@done` is inferred `bool` and the package loads.

    A role `$view` is the path where a checker may skip full typing (a role view
    may read `$actor`, whose row type resolves later), so it is the path where an
    inferred parameter could silently degrade to "anything goes". Attack: an
    authenticated member passes a value the inferred type does not admit, hoping
    the unenforced role path accepts it. §12.1 step 3 parses arguments against
    the inferred shape, so the JSON string "yes" does not decode as `bool` and
    the request is malformed. The role path and the public path therefore agree:
    same inference, same enforcement.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.roleviewparam@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      accounts: {
        $key: "id"
        id: "text"
        enabled: "bool = true"
      }
      tasks: {
        $key: "id"
        id: "text"
        done: "bool"
      }
      $auth: {
        token: {
          $credential: "text"
          $verify: "$credential"
          $actor: "/accounts[$proof]"
        }
      }
      $roles: {
        member: {
          $auth: "token"
          $members: ".accounts[:a | a.enabled]"
          by_state: {
            // No $params: @done is inferred `bool` from `t.done == @done` (§10.1).
            $view: ".tasks[:t | t.done == @done] { id }"
          }
        }
      }
    }
    $data: {
      accounts: {
        alice: {}
      }
      tasks: {
        t1: { done: false }
        t2: { done: true }
      }
    }
  }

  steps: [
    { connect: "c1", authenticate: { role: "member", auth: "token", credential: "alice" } }
    { watch: "member.by_state", args: { done: true }, on: "c1", id: "w1",
      expect_init: { value: [ { id: "t2" } ] } }
    { watch: "member.by_state", args: { done: false }, on: "c1", id: "w2",
      expect_init: { value: [ { id: "t1" } ] } }
    // The inferred `bool` binds the role path exactly as it binds the public one.
    { watch: "member.by_state", args: { done: "yes" }, on: "c1", id: "w3",
      expect: { outcome: rejected, violates: ["#clients", "§12.1"] } }
  ]
}
